# An overloaded core function must mangle to the SAME C symbol regardless of
# whether `core` is opened — the mangled name is a property of the callee, not
# of open-state (#137). Here core is imported (loaded) but NOT opened, and the
# calls are qualified; under --no-implicit this used to risk a bare `rae_log`
# C symbol. The overloads (String vs Any) each resolve to their own symbol.
import core
func main() {
  core.log("text")
  core.log(42)
  core.log(true)
}
